**Answer:** Given point P is outside the plane of triangle ABC, with PO perpendicular to plane ABC at foot O, and PA=PB=PC, it can be proven that triangle POA is congruent to triangle POB is congruent to triangle POC, thereby proving OA=OB=OC. The point O that satisfies this property is the circumcenter of triangle ABC.  
Proof: Connect AO and extend it to intersect BC at D; connect BO and extend it to intersect AC at E;  
Since PA is perpendicular to PB, and PA is perpendicular to PC, thus PA is perpendicular to plane PBC, which means PA is perpendicular to BC;  
Since PO is perpendicular to plane ABC, thus PO is perpendicular to BC, which means BC is perpendicular to plane PAO,  
Thus AO is perpendicular to BC, i.e., AD is perpendicular to BC;  
